## Node identity and runtime flags for mcl_rag.
-name ${MCL_NODE_NAME}@${MCL_NODE_HOST}
-setcookie ${MCL_COOKIE}
## Distribution is bound to loopback (mcl-rag#32). The node name above says who
## this node is, not where it listens: under host networking an unbound node
## listens on every interface, and the lab measured this one on 0.0.0.0.
## Nothing off the box uses distribution, the mesh is QUIC, and epmd is bounded
## beside this by ERL_EPMD_ADDRESS in the image.
-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}

+K true

## Async thread pool. Raise it only if this service does real file or port I/O;
## for CPU-bound work the schedulers are the resource that matters and this flag
## is not on that path.
+A 8
